        "root_concepts": "[planarity, treewidth]",
        "section": "mathematics-physics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Planarity and Graph Structure",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PLANARITY                         TREEWIDTH\n   (geometric structure)             (decomposition structure)\n   -------------------------         ----------------------------------\n   drawable with no edge crossings   \"how far from being a tree?\"\n        |                                 |\n        |  Euler:  V - E + F = 2           |  tree (tw=1) -> series-parallel (tw=2)\n        |  forbidden minors: K5, K3,3      |  -> ... -> clique K_n (tw = n-1)\n        v                                  v\n   LINEAR-TIME planarity test        BOUNDED treewidth => DP solves NP-hard\n   (Hopcroft-Tarjan, Boyer-Myrvold)  problems in poly time (Courcelle's theorem)"
    },
    {
